1
00:00:00,314 --> 00:00:02,884
(Sheldon:)I feel no better now
than when I left.

2
00:00:02,883 --> 00:00:04,453
(Amy:)But you still
accomplished something.

3
00:00:04,452 --> 00:00:06,152
(Leonard:)Yeah. If you had
told anyone

4
00:00:06,153 --> 00:00:08,323
(Leonard:)that you were going away
on a train by yourself

5
00:00:08,322 --> 00:00:10,922
(Leonard:)across the country, do you
know what they would have said?

6
00:00:10,925 --> 00:00:12,955
(Sheldon:)That I couldn't do it?
Exactly.

7
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:15,490
Right after they said, "Yay!"

8
00:00:16,864 --> 00:00:18,494
(Amy:)But you did do it.

9
00:00:18,499 --> 00:00:20,629
(Amy:)So what if it didn't
all go your way?

10
00:00:20,635 --> 00:00:22,905
(Amy:)That's what makes it
an adventure.

11
00:00:22,903 --> 00:00:25,003
(Sheldon:)That's a good point.

12
00:00:25,006 --> 00:00:28,536
Yeah, I'm a lot like
Gandalf the Grey.

13
00:00:28,542 --> 00:00:30,842
(Sheldon:)He fought the Balrog and emerged

14
00:00:30,845 --> 00:00:33,475
(Sheldon:)stronger than ever
as Gandalf the White.

15
00:00:33,481 --> 00:00:36,081
(Sheldon:)I was robbed
of my phone and pants,

16
00:00:36,083 --> 00:00:38,383
(Sheldon:)and I, too,
came back stronger.

17
00:00:38,386 --> 00:00:40,286
(Sheldon:)And whiter, too,
'cause I wasn't

18
00:00:40,287 --> 00:00:43,087
(Sheldon:)in direct sunlight
for six weeks.

19
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:46,330
(Amy:)See? This trip
was good for you.

20
00:00:46,327 --> 00:00:47,957
(Sheldon:)Indeed.

21
00:00:47,962 --> 00:00:51,192
(Sheldon:)I was the world's
smartest caterpillar.

22
00:00:51,198 --> 00:00:54,998
(Sheldon:)And then after pupating
in our nation's railway system,

23
00:00:55,002 --> 00:00:56,572
(Sheldon:)I've burst forth

24
00:00:56,570 --> 00:01:00,020
(Sheldon:)as the world's
smartest butterfly.

